{# Brutalist enterprise type stack:
     Saira Condensed — condensed industrial display (weights 500–900), used for billboard moments (H1, hero numbers, section headlines)
     Archivo         — regular family for body + mid-display
     JetBrains Mono  — regulator-credible mono for compliance frameworks, timestamps, signed-evidence callouts
   These three are loaded site-wide. Per-element font choice comes from the `--v-display / --v-sans / --v-mono` tokens in src/input.css.

   Self-hosted, NOT loaded from fonts.googleapis.com / fonts.gstatic.com.
   A webfont request to Google transmits the visitor's IP to Google and cannot
   be justified under legitimate interest for a German audience (LG München I,
   3 O 17493/20); it also happens before any consent decision, which § 25
   TDDDG does not allow. The .woff2 files and fonts/fonts.css are generated by
   `python3 scripts/fetch_google_fonts.py` — latin + latin-ext subsets only.

   Load strategy:
     1. The stylesheet is same-origin and ~12 KB, so it is a plain
        render-blocking <link>. The old media="print" onload swap existed to
        keep a third-party origin off the critical path; with no third party
        left it only bought FOUT.
     2. The two faces that paint above the fold are preloaded so they download
        in parallel with the CSS instead of after it.
     3. `font-display: swap` lives in every @font-face in fonts.css. #}
